Another thought (although it might not be totally related) is the
configuration of your NIC (network interface card).  I've experienced
problems on HPUX systems with multiple NICs running extremely slow in bootup
and then run very slowly in excuting commands.  This slow down is such that
one would think the system is hung --- real noticeable.  The problem was
caused by the NICs being incorrectly configured and/or other network issues
such as having mismatched network port speeds, i.e full-duplex at the
netport and half-duplex and the NIC.  Although what I experienced was on
HPUX systems, I'm sure that this occurrence can happen UNIX-wide.  So it's
something to look at.

Some reference commands:  lanscan, netstat, ioscan

Keith Kepner
kkepner@gte.net

