You could start with mt:

	mt(1)

	NAME
  	mt - Magnetic tape manipulating program

	SYNOPSIS

	  mt [-f tape_device] command [count]

	  The mt program gives commands to a magnetic tape drive.

Basically, configure the drive so that it automatically loads the next
tape when unloaded (Sequential mode). Whenever an "mt unload" is issued,
the current tape should get rewound/unloaded and the next tape loaded
into place. You may need to specify the -f parameter if the drive is
NOT  /dev/rmt0.

This works well if you are just performing simple backups of separate
volumes to separate tapes. If you start getting into using the bar code
reader, multi-tape backups, or want to control the robot directly, you
will need separate software. I don't think anything in the standard
DU/T64 command set would help in those cases.

PS - Get a firware update for the DLT891 ASAP if you haven't already.
We've had the CPQ Dude (formerly DEC Tech) in several times in the past
couple months to replace the leader on our drive. Turns out there is a
bug in the firmware that can cause this. An update should be available
from your friendly neighborhood CPQ Dude.
-- 

