Should work with no problem.  Neither DUMP nor TAR create any type of file
system
on the tape, merely write a stream on to the media.  Confirm by writing a
small file system
with dump -f /dev/tapename /smallfilesystemname
or tar a directory of a few files with
tar cvf /dev/tapename /home/testdir/*

the tapename is probably something like /dev/rmt0h or /dev/nrmt0h.
The directories and filesystems are fictitious.  You'll have to find one
that really exists.

To check your tape:
  on the dump tape:
      restore -i -f /dev/tapename    (see man page for details)

on the tar tape:
     tar xvf /dev/tapename|more

Luck :)
