In article <k0r9oe6uop.fsf@dylan.ucsf.edu>, David T. Blake wrote:
>
>DecUnix has the Xserver compiled into the kernel, and Dec only
>supports a few cards. In my case, I think only Powerstorm cards
>are supported for TrueColor under DecUnix, and they cost more
>than a new PentiumII just for the video card.
>
>Or are you supposing that I could compile the Matrox Mystique 
>driver for Alpha linux XFree86 and have it work as a kernel space
>X server for DecUnix ?? 
>

The X server included with Digital UNIX, /usr/bin/X11/Xdec, is a
standard COFF executable, not a kernel module. Thus it runs in
user space, and can in theory be replaced by another X server.
The procedure for accessing the video hardware could be somewhat
different on Digital UNIX than on Linux, so the XFree86 code
might not work unmodified. The XFree86 developers might be
