"Peter" <peter@j9.freeuk.com> writes:
> I am using VMSTAT to monitor my systems memory. How do I tell if it is low
> on memory ?.

Do a 'vmstat -P' and have a look at the Managed Pages Break Down section.
Roughly speaking, free means free mem, active + inactive means in use by
processes, wired means diverse unswappable system memory, ubc is the unified
buffer cache. It can be a bit tricky though to exactly define what constitutes
'low' free memory.

Perhaps a more pragmatic approach would be to run 'vmstat 1' for a while and
see if the system swaps a lot (pin colunm). If it does, you're running low
on memory.


Cheers,
Sander
