Gaylord Holder (holder@phy.ucsf.edu) wrote:

: I've been having problems with networking on a 600au running 4.0Dp3.
: It was running 100Mbs full duplex and hanging on nfs service.  I
: changed it to half duplex and the reliablity and speed seem to have
: increased.  What's going on?

Well, you cannot run full-duplex on a shared wire - your cable should
go straight from your 600au to a switch (no, you cannot use a hub).
You also must have both your 600au and the switch port serving it 
running full-duplex. Since autonegotiation for full-duplex often fails,
it is a good idea to have both ends locked in 100mbit full-duplex mode.

/Serge.P

