I got answers from two experts.The problem is solved.

Answer one:
Maybe your nameserver (DNS server) has a problem. CDE tries to
talk to some components (rpc.ttdbservd for example) over the network.
When your DNS server is down or misconfigured, it cannot resolve the
names and hence waits until a timeout occurs.

So: Check your DNS server and configuration.



********************************************************************************

Answer two:
Probably you problem is related to problem in your local IP.
This problem is very common when there are problems with tle Ip address,
/etc/host file modified (o corrupted), /etc/rc.config mofied manually.







