Nothing.  You can get bits and pieces to make you life easier, but I've
not seen anything that you will be happy with if you're used to managing
a large cluster with one command to SYSMAN.  Plan on increasing your
manpower.  

OBTW, there is NO device management for tapes other than to
prevent sharing while a file is open on a tape.  So if you write a
backup to a tape and don't immediatley phycially dismount it, anything
could be on it.

>Question: Is it too much to ask for solutions that can deal
>with VMS, and various unices (Tru64, Solaris, Linux, etc.),
>and possibly NT (ugh).

Yep.  For users, all UNIX are about the same, for programmers they're a
bit different, and for system admins all UNIX are completly different. 
Look into products like Tivoli, but don't swallow the glossies whole.

