Im not up on VMS, but as far as unix admin tools, AIX has smit (system
management interface tool) which is a standard, text or gui based tool.
You can do more from this single tool than you can from any other I have
seen. I prefer solaris myself which has admintool.

The reason you dont have a be all and end all tool is because in the
unix world you have a large choice on which products you wish to use
because different products will suit different critera and sites.
eg for disk management in solaris I can use the standard format, newfs
command line tools or use solstice disksuite or veritas or something
else entirely.

If you do want a "one interface" you can look at BMC-Patrol or Tivoli
etc which are highly customisable (but generally carry a hefty price
tag).

I cant see there being the necessity to get more manpower unless you
hire people who dont have a decent skill level in the operating system
you use.

