Then, try pdftops to get the file into a ps format, and
then read it with some version of ghostscript/ghostview/gv/ggv.

Ghostscript does font-lookups for all fonts available on the
machine (that are in the ghostscript directories). Adobe does
it a little better in that it will perform somewhat intelligent
substitutions for fonts that are not found.

If you do lots of pdf/ps work, you are really limiting
yourself if you maintain that you can only read files with
Adobe software (especially since their software is not up to
snuff).

