Password shadowing for Tru64 Unix is only available as part of the C2 
(enhanced) security configuration that comes as a standard part of the
distribution. Before configuring C2, please read the manual carefully 
and be aware of the changes that C2 makes to the day to day
administration 
of the system. This is /particularly/ true when running NIS.

The vipw program simply runs the mkpasswd program on exit, creating
the hashed database (passwd.pag,dir) files. These are /not/ shadow
files and are only used to speed lookup of information stored in
the ascii passwd file.

Alan Davis
Tru64 Unix Consultant

