Hi,

forget about all this init.d, rc.2/3/n stuff. Just add an new (last) entry in 
/etc/inittab e.g.

own:23:wait:/etc/rc.myownstuff > blah blah

in this rc.myownstuff you can specify all you want to start.
This technique works on all systems with an inittab, regardless where the 
rc.2/3/n are located - don't fiddle in system directories!

