<37331F14.E52D240B@sbcm.com>...
I cut it down...
>5) The number given to the links in
>2) and 3) determines the order of
>execution; for "S" scripts higher
>numbered scripts are executed later;
>you probably don't want, e.g., samba
>to run before networking is up and running.

This is true so long as the number is less than 100,
 the order is ASCII sort order, and this caused me
all sorts of problems until I twigged.
S100 will execute between S10 and S11 unless you
change them all.

