Stephen:
	The reason you're getting the "_end" unresolved symbol
	is because your link line is creating a shared library
	and not an executable.  Please change the "-shared"
	flag to "-call_shared" so that you'll be building an
	executable.  The "man 3 end" manpage has more about
	the symbols like end.

	Also, please remove the "/usr/ccs/lib/crt0.o" from your
	link line.  The cc driver inserts it in the link line
	where it's needed.

	You also need to put your cltest.o object file earlier
	in the link line.  If it references symbols that are defined
	in other libraries, they will never get linked in unless
	cltest.o is seen by the linker before those libraries.

	One last nit, as of the DIGITAL UNIX V4.0 release, for
	C applications, you no longer need to link with libots.
	All _Ots* symbols used by DEC C are defined in libc.

Joe Mario
Compaq Tru64 Development Environment

	

