The complete lack of detail on machines and operating systems involved
make this very difficult to answer, but if the machine which has the
backup medium is DIGITAL UNIX, then vdump will work with UFS and NFS
filesystems. I've never tried with the NFS server machine being Solaris,
but I can't see that would make a difference for a data disk.

Incidentally, the "dump" command on Solaris is "ufsdump". You can
backup to a remote tape drive with 

ufsdump 0uf - /dev/rdsk/c0t0d0s0 | rsh axpj 'dd of=/dev/nrmt0h bs=32k'

This works from Solaris to D.U. V4.0D (and the equivalent should work
between most Unix pairs. Prior to D.U. V4.0D, I used to do

ufsdump 0uf rem_node:/dev/nrmt0h /dev/rdsk/c0t0d0s0

but something changed in rmt when I upgraded.
Hope this helps,
John Hill
