Louis Desjardins wrote:

> I would like to know how can I make my serveur respond to a new segment on
> the network. I would like to bind the new network on the same network card
> (1 card, 2 network). Each of them as it's route.
>
> Thank for you help.
>
> Louis-Steve

Hi,
All you have to do is find out the IP address of the router to the new
segment. Here is an example:

Say your server is at address 167.76.43.2, the network or segment you want to
get to is 57. The router would have two network interface cards, one each
network, one on the network your server is on and one on the 57 network. The
router would have addresses for example 167.76.43.1 and 167.76.57.1 .  In
order to get to the segment 57 network you would do a route add command:
route add -net 57 167.76.43.1 . The statement says that to get to segment 57
you go to address 167.76.43.1 .

Hope that helps.

