  phenix1@my-dejanews.com wrote:

> NIS isn't C2 compliants


And was completely wrong.

Digital UNIX 4.0D works just fine with C2 + NIS.  (As long as you
don't mind that you cannot log in to an NIS-based account if the
master server is down.)

The steps for setting up C2+NIS are found in section 9.3 of the
Security book, along with back-out procedures.

see:

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/
       base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V40D_HTML/AQ0R2DTE/TITLE.HTM


As for getting in in the first place, if booting to single-user does
not work, you'll have to use the install media.  Boot it, mount up
the root fs and go in and do some manual editing.

Various tips are given in Ch 14 (Trusted System Troubleshooting) on
how things should look and how to check them.  Your symptoms match
a problem we had where the conversion to the trusted db failed. Check
out root's authcap (/tcb/bin/edauth root).

Michael Kellen
