In article <373707ad.5430639@192.9.200.16>, John Allen
<john.allen@geonet-tech.com> wrote:

>I've been using dump to backup data on my Alphastation running DU
>V4.0e.  Occasionally, the system will hang when I'm performing a dump
>during work hours(ie, when users are accessing files).

If by "hang" you mean the system becomes non-responsive, but after a
bit it comes back to life, that might be an overloaded situation and
dump is just pushing the system a bit too hard for your needs.

However, if by "hang" you mean the system is wedged and must be
rebooted, then nothing should do that (except maybe running out of swap
space; but there should console messages about low swap space).  Again,
if it is wedged, then that should be reported to one of the customer
support centers and crash dumps supplied so that it can be analyzed and
corrected.  If possible provide instructions on how to reproduce it.



